<title>USA: ADVISORY-IMF says SDR rates delayed.</title>
<headline>ADVISORY-IMF says SDR rates delayed.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The International Monetary Fund said Friday the daily SDR rates, except for the U.S. dollar rate, were temporarily unavailable due to technical problems. Earlier, the IMF reported the exchange value of the U.S. dollar against the SDR on Friday was 1.38779, versus 1.39039 Thursday and 1.20635 on July 1, 1974.</p>
<p>On Thursday, the IMF reported the following currency values against the SDR (July 1, 1974 rates in parentheses):</p>
<p> Deutsche Mark     2.39703   (3.06809)</p>
<p> French Franc	8.09972   (5.82126)</p>
<p> Japanese Yen	155.585   (343.773)</p>
<p> Pounds Sterling   0.851381   (0.505474)</p>
<p> Australian Dlr    1.84843   (0.809889)</p>
<p> Aust Schilling    16.8738   (22.0097)</p>
<p> Belgian Franc     49.4388   (45.9249)</p>
<p> Canadian Dlr	1.92194   (1.16295)</p>
<p> Danish Kroner     9.12026   (7.23304)</p>
<p> Indonesian Rupiah   n/a     (501.291)</p>
<p> Iranian Rial	2449.84   (81.6734)</p>
<p> Italian Lire	2360.95   (779.746)</p>
<p> Kuwait Dinar	0.420885   (0.351685)</p>
<p> Dutch Guilder     2.69624   (3.20316)</p>
<p> Norwegian Kroner  9.97396   (6.59386)</p>
<p> Saudi Arab Riyal  5.20701   (4.25788)</p>
<p> S.A. Rand	   6.25745   (0.80200)</p>
<p> Spanish Peseta    202.719   (69.0742)</p>
<p> Swedish Kronor    10.8103   (5.31489)</p>
<p> Swiss Franc	 2.00772   (3.19548)</p>
<p> U.A.E. Dirham     5.10412   (4.76057)</p>
<p>S.A. Rand July 2, Australian Dlr Aug 1, Canadian Dlr July 2, Indonesian Rupiah July 19, Iranian Rial July 22, Saudi Riyal Aug 9, all 1974. Swiss Franc Sept 16, 1975.</p>
